# Add to your user crontab with: crontab -e
# Use ABSOLUTE paths to the venv's python and the script.
# Adjust the path (here /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote) to your install.
#
# Configuration (folder, categories, etc.) is read from the .env file next to
# the script, so no variables are needed here. To override on the command line
# instead, append flags, e.g. ... kindle_to_onenote.py --folder "Scribe Notes"

# Every 15 minutes
*/15 * * * * /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/.venv/bin/python /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle_to_onenote.py >> /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle.log 2>&1

# Every 5 minutes
# */5 * * * * /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/.venv/bin/python /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle_to_onenote.py >> /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle.log 2>&1

# Every minute
# * * * * * /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/.venv/bin/python /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle_to_onenote.py >> /home/USER/scribe-to-onenote/kindle.log 2>&1
